CLI-VERSION|cli|--version prints sxr and the runtime package version.|test_smoke.py::test_version|VERSION
CLI-PARSERS|cli|Find and skills produce equivalent results through fast entry points and Typer routing.|test_find.py::test_fast_cli*;test_find_current.py::test_fast_cli*;test_skills.py::test_paths_aliases_and_both_parsers;test_find_integrity.py::test_usage_errors*;test_find_paths.py::test_path_limits*|LIST-provider
CLI-FLAG-POSITIONS|cli|Shared provider, project, output, time and discovery flags work before or after the command; clean also accepts group-level flags.|test_file_selection.py::test_explicit_file*;test_secrets_cli.py::test_clean_flag_positions*;test_find_integrity.py::test_coverage_and_root_flags*;test_scope.py::test_before_today*|LIST-provider
CLI-CONFLICTS|cli|Conflicting providers and provider-specific discovery flags return usage errors with a useful diagnostic.|test_secrets_cli.py::test_conflicting_provider_flags*;test_find_integrity.py::test_usage_errors*;test_file_selection.py::test_file_validation*|
CLI-NEGATIVE-LIMIT|cli|Negative row limits are rejected with exit 2, consistent with find and skills. This is a consistency expectation beyond the documented 0 and positive values.|test_find_integrity.py::test_usage_errors*;test_skills.py::test_bad_skill_flags*|USAGE-negative-limit-
